                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "I got the original Professor Fizzwizzle for Christmas on a CD back in 2009. I bought this one off of Big Fish Games in 2013. Even though it's a kids game, it is still, hands down, the best puzzle game I've ever played. I bought this game on Steam a few days ago while it was on sale for the sole purpose of writing this review. I've easily played this game for over 750 hours (not on Steam obviously) and it's never gotten boring. The advanced level set is incredibly difficult and ingenious, and even the regular set gets really hard the further you get into it\n\nThe real crown is the level editor, and that's where most of my hours come from. The editor is super easy to understand and use, and i love making levels, even if nobody will see them since the fanbase is long dead :P\n\nIf you are looking for a puzzle game to last you a long time and the story doesn't matter much to you (it is a kids game after all), I would highly recommend this game. \n\nEasy 10/10",
